{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"complex system complex system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md","fileName":"Complex System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Complex System","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Systems Foundations]] [[Emergent Systems]] [[Emergent Game Narrative]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Systems Foundations","Emergent Systems","Emergent Game Narrative","Complicated Process","Emergence","Systems Thinking","Possibility Space","Emergent Story","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"complex system complex system","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Complex System.md","fileName":"Complex System.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Complex System","heading":"Complex System","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A complex system contains interacting parts whose effects loop back and alter later system behavior. Unlike a [[Complicated Process]], it is not adequately described as a long linear sequence.\n\nFeedback makes complex systems history-dependent, adaptive, and capable of [[Emergence]]. Their behavior is best understood by combining part-level detail with a view of loops, the whole, and the surrounding context through [[Systems Thinking]].\n\nFor games, complexity comes from relationships among verbs and objects rather than their sheer quantity. Strong interactions create a [[Possibility Space]] that cannot be completely plotted in advance and can produce varied [[Emergent Story|emergent stories]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Syste